	In order to write scrolls reliably, you must have already identified
the scroll you are trying to write.  Usually this means having read the scroll
in question.  The number of charges a particular scroll will drain from the
magic marker is dependent on the type of scroll you are trying to write; a
scroll of light may only use 5 charges, while a scroll of genocide averages
about 30.  The blessed/cursed state of the scroll created depends on the
blessed/cursed state of both the magic marker and the blank scroll used.
Scrolls can be erased by #dipping them into any body of water (fountains and
moats, for example.)

>>>completing quests given to you
>>Oh, how do you get these?  Is this what the Oracle of Delphi is for?
>I don't know how to get them. I know they are given to you as you get deeper
>into the dungeon, but I never got down far enough.

	When you reach a certain level of the dungeon, you will hear your
former mentor pleading for your assistance for something.  Searching around
that particular level will reveal a magical portal that will transport you to
your mentor's locale.  (hint:  after passing through the portal, take one step
and search until you find the other portal.  This is the way out once you've
completed the quest.)

	Once your mentor has charged you to retrieve whatever it is he/she
wants, search about his level until you find a staircase and follow it to your
destiny.

	When you find and slay Nalzok, the Ultimate Evil/Bubba, Prince of
Thieves/King Slimeball, pick up the bell it dropped in addition to whatever it
was you were supposed to be looking for.  You'll need it later.

